<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Acco</h1><p class="st-meta">1800 BCE – 1150 BCE (approx.) · capital Acco</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Acco, a Canaanite harbour town on the bay of Haifa, a vassal of Egypt in the Amarna age and forerunner of the later port of Acre.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Akka grew on Tel Akko, beside the mouth of the Na'aman river, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-bronze-age">Middle Bronze Age</a>, when it was surrounded by massive earth ramparts. It is named in Egyptian execration texts and in the list of towns conquered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thutmose-iii">Thutmose III</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>As a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/egyptian-empire-new-kingdom">Egyptian Empire New Kingdom</a> it was governed by local kings who traded with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean</a> through its harbour. Its rulers Zurata and Zatatna appear in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amarna-letters">Amarna letters</a>, accused by neighbours of plotting with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt's</a> enemies.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Acco's Canaanite kingdom ended in the upheavals of the 12th century BCE. The city later came under Phoenician rule, was renamed <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/barca">Ptolemais</a> by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ptolemaic-empire">Ptolemaic Empire</a>, and survives as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acre">Acre</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="city state, 1800 BCE – 1150 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M60 54 H66"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">city state</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Anatolia and the Levant</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:23.88%;width:12.94%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1800 BCE – 1150 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century-bce">19th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/12th-century-bce">12th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Acco</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Zurata, Zatatna</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Canaanite religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Canaanite, Akkadian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/israel">Israel</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Akka, Canaanite Acre</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-1475&amp;focus=acco" aria-label="Acco on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5582 1051 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Acco lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5863 1489h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5902 1307h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5902 1307h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Israel. <a href="/atlas?year=-1475&amp;focus=acco">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

